IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) Part 4.2 -- trust money, as it touches the lawyer and the client whose money his firm holds:
-- what is trust money (s 129), the written warning for money that is not (s 134), where each kind of trust money must go (ss 137-
-- 143), its protection from the firm's creditors (s 145), when the firm may pay its own costs out of it (s 144(2)(b), General
-- Rules r 42), and the client's trust account statements (General Rules r 52).
--
-- SEAT: the lawyer (Daniel, an employee solicitor at Swan & Partners from 2020 to 2031). The duties in Part 4.2 fall on the "law
-- practice"; for him they are what his firm must do with a client's money, which he handles as an associate (s 135(2): trust money
-- "may be dealt with only by the law practice or an associate of the law practice"). The civil penalties fall on the firm.
--
-- Provisions covered: [Uniform Law] ss 128 ("controlled money", "transit money", "general trust account"), 129, 134, 135, 137,
-- 138(1), 139(1), 140(1), 141(1), 142(1), 143, 144(2)(b), 145; [General Rules] rr 42(3)-(5), 52(1), (4), (5).
--
-- Edition: as in lpul-practice.l4 -- [Uniform Law] mrdoc 46913 at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_46913.txt; [General Rules]
-- mrdoc 45732, version 00-a0-02, at ../../../legal-profession-uniform-general-rules-2015/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45732.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the territorial reach of Part 4.2 (s 130: the firm is taken to have its only office in WA); trust records,
-- receipting, reconciliation and the cash books (s 147, General Rules rr 35-51); external examination and investigation
-- (Divisions 3, 4); irregularity reports (s 154); unclaimed money (s 167: jurisdictional legislation, not deposited); the lien
-- (s 144(2)(a)); commercial clients' own directions about statements (General Rules r 53); the expired transitional r 52(6);
-- fidelity cover (Part 4.5).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) -- trust money`

§§ `s 129 -- is it trust money`

-- [Uniform Law] s 129(1): "trust money is money entrusted to a law practice in the course of or in connection with the provision
-- of legal services by the law practice, and includes -- (a) money received by the law practice on account of legal costs in
-- advance of providing the services; and (b) controlled money ...; and (c) transit money ...; and (d) money ... that is the
-- subject of a power exercisable by the law practice or an associate ... to deal with the money for or on behalf of another
-- person."
-- s 129(2): "the following money is not trust money -- (a) money received by a law practice for legal services that have been
-- provided and in respect of which a bill has been given to the client; (b) money entrusted to or held by a law practice for or
-- in connection with -- (i) a managed investment scheme; or (ii) mortgage financing; undertaken by the law practice; (c) money
-- received ... for or in connection with a financial service it provides [under, or as representative of, an Australian
-- financial services licence]; (d) money received by a law practice for investment purposes unless -- (i) the law practice
-- received the money in the ordinary course of legal practice and primarily in connection with the provision of legal services
-- at the direction of the client; and (ii) the investment is or is to be made in the ordinary course of legal practice and for
-- the ancillary purpose of maintaining or enhancing the value of the money or property; (e) money determined under section 152
-- not to be trust money; (f) money declared by the Uniform Rules not to be trust money."
-- s 128: "controlled money means money ... in respect of which the law practice has a written direction to deposit the money in
-- an account (other than a general trust account) over which the law practice has or will have exclusive control"; "transit money
-- means money received by a law practice subject to instructions to pay or deliver it to a third party, other than an associate".
DECLARE `What the money is` IS ONE OF
    `money on account of legal costs in advance`                      -- s 129(1)(a)
    `controlled money`                                                -- s 129(1)(b), s 128
    `transit money`                                                   -- s 129(1)(c), s 128
    `money subject to a power to deal with it for another person`    -- s 129(1)(d)
    `other money entrusted in connection with the firm's legal services`
    `payment for legal services provided and billed`                  -- s 129(2)(a)
    `money for a managed investment scheme or mortgage financing the firm undertakes` -- s 129(2)(b)
    `money for a financial service under an Australian financial services licence`     -- s 129(2)(c)
    `money for investment purposes`                                   -- s 129(2)(d)

DECLARE `The money` HAS
    `what it is`                                                     IS A `What the money is`
    `received in the ordinary course of legal practice at the client's direction` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 129(2)(d)(i)
    `invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS A BOOLEAN            -- s 129(2)(d)(ii)
    `determined under s 152 not to be trust money`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 129(2)(e)
    `declared by the Uniform Rules not to be trust money`            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 129(2)(f)
    `received in cash`                                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 143
    `a written direction to deal with it otherwise`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 137(a), s 142

-- The s 129(2)(c)-(f) exclusions, which s 134(2) calls "non-trust money".
GIVEN `the money` IS A `The money`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`non-trust money under s 134` MEANS
        `the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `money for a financial service under an Australian financial services licence`
    OR  (    `the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `money for investment purposes`
         AND (NOT (    `the money`'s `received in the ordinary course of legal practice at the client's direction`
                   AND `the money`'s `invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value`)))
    OR  `the money`'s `determined under s 152 not to be trust money`
    OR  `the money`'s `declared by the Uniform Rules not to be trust money`

@export Is this money that my firm holds for the client trust money (Uniform Law s 129)?
GIVEN `the money` IS A `The money` @desc The money and why your firm holds it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this money trust money` IF
        (NOT `non-trust money under s 134` `the money`)
    AND (NOT (`the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `payment for legal services provided and billed`))
    AND (NOT (`the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `money for a managed investment scheme or mortgage financing the firm undertakes`))

§§ `s 134 -- the warning for money that is not trust money`

-- [Uniform Law] s 134(1): "If a law practice receives or holds money that is non-trust money (other than money for the payment
-- of legal costs due to the law practice), it must give the person who provided the money written notice that -- (a) the money
-- will not be treated as trust money; and (b) the money is not subject to the provisions relating to trust money in this Law or
-- the Uniform Rules; and (c) a claim against the fidelity fund of this jurisdiction cannot be made in respect of the money. Civil
-- penalty: 100 penalty units." s 134(2): "non-trust money is money that is not trust money ... because of section 129(2)(c),
-- (d), (e) or (f)."
@export Must my firm warn the client in writing that this money is not trust money and not covered by the fidelity fund (Uniform Law s 134)?
GIVEN `the money` IS A `The money` @desc The money and why your firm holds it
      `it pays legal costs due to my firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is for the payment of legal costs already due to your firm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my firm warn the client that this is not trust money` IF
    `non-trust money under s 134` `the money` AND (NOT `it pays legal costs due to my firm`)

§§ `ss 135, 137-143 -- where the client's money must go`

-- [Uniform Law] s 135(1): "A law practice must deal with trust money in accordance with this Law and the Uniform Rules and not
-- otherwise. Civil penalty: 50 penalty units."
-- s 137: the practice "must deposit trust money (other than cash) into the law practice's general trust account as soon as
-- practicable after receiving it unless -- (a) the law practice has a written direction by a person legally entitled to provide
-- it to deal with the money otherwise ...; or (b) the money is controlled money or transit money; or (c) the money is the subject
-- of a power". s 138(1): it must "(a) hold trust money deposited in the law practice's general trust account exclusively for the
-- person on whose behalf it is received; and (b) disburse the trust money only in accordance with a direction given by the
-- person".
-- s 139(1): "As soon as practicable after receiving controlled money, a law practice must deposit the money in the account
-- specified in the written direction". s 140(1): transit money must be paid or delivered "as required by the instructions ...
-- within the period (if any) specified in the instructions, or else as soon as practicable". s 141(1): trust money subject to a
-- power must be "dealt with only in accordance with that power". s 142(1): a written direction must be complied with "within the
-- period specified in the direction, or otherwise, as soon as practicable".
-- s 143(1): "A law practice must deposit all trust money received in the form of cash (other than controlled money) in the law
-- practice's general trust account as soon as practicable after receiving the money, even if it has a written direction to deal
-- with it in some other way. Once deposited, the money may be dealt with in accordance with the written direction." s 143(2):
-- controlled money in cash goes to "a controlled money account".
DECLARE `Where the money goes` IS ONE OF
    `not trust money: the trust money provisions do not govern it`
    `into the controlled money account named in the written direction, as soon as practicable (ss 139(1), 143(2))`
    `into the general trust account as soon as practicable because it is cash, even if a written direction says otherwise; then as the direction says (s 143(1))`
    `paid or delivered as instructed, within the time set or as soon as practicable (s 140(1))`
    `dealt with only in accordance with the power (s 141(1))`
    `dealt with as the written direction says, within the time set or as soon as practicable (ss 137(a), 142(1))`
    `into the general trust account as soon as practicable, held only for the client and paid out only on the client's direction (ss 137, 138)`

@export Where must my firm put the client's money (Uniform Law ss 137-143)?
GIVEN `the money` IS A `The money` @desc The money, why your firm holds it and how it was received
GIVETH A `Where the money goes`
DECIDE `Where must my firm put the client's money` IS
    IF (NOT `Is this money trust money` `the money`)
    THEN `not trust money: the trust money provisions do not govern it`
    ELSE IF `the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `controlled money`
         THEN `into the controlled money account named in the written direction, as soon as practicable (ss 139(1), 143(2))`
         ELSE IF `the money`'s `received in cash`
              THEN `into the general trust account as soon as practicable because it is cash, even if a written direction says otherwise; then as the direction says (s 143(1))`
              ELSE IF `the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `transit money`
                   THEN `paid or delivered as instructed, within the time set or as soon as practicable (s 140(1))`
                   ELSE IF `the money`'s `what it is` EQUALS `money subject to a power to deal with it for another person`
                        THEN `dealt with only in accordance with the power (s 141(1))`
                        ELSE IF `the money`'s `a written direction to deal with it otherwise`
                             THEN `dealt with as the written direction says, within the time set or as soon as practicable (ss 137(a), 142(1))`
                             ELSE `into the general trust account as soon as practicable, held only for the client and paid out only on the client's direction (ss 137, 138)`

§§ `s 145 -- protection from the firm's creditors`

-- [Uniform Law] s 145(1): "Money standing to the credit of a trust account maintained by a law practice is not available for the
-- payment of debts of the law practice or any of its associates." (2): it "is not liable to be attached or taken in execution for
-- satisfying a judgment against the law practice or any of its associates." (3): "This section does not apply to money to which a
-- law practice or associate is entitled."
@export Is the money in my firm's trust account safe from the firm's creditors and from judgments against the firm or me (Uniform Law s 145)?
GIVEN `my firm or an associate is entitled to the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your firm or one of its associates (such as you) is itself entitled to the money
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the trust money safe from my firm's creditors` IF
    NOT `my firm or an associate is entitled to the money`

§§ `s 144(2)(b), General Rules r 42 -- may my firm pay its costs out of trust money`

-- [Uniform Law] s 144(2)(b): the practice may "withdraw money for payment to the law practice's account for legal costs owing to
-- the practice if the relevant procedures or requirements specified in the Uniform Rules ... are complied with".
-- [General Rules] r 42(3): it may withdraw "if the law practice has given the person a bill relating to the money and referring to
-- the proposed withdrawal, and -- (a) if the person does not, at the end of the period of 7 business days after the person was
-- given the bill, object to the amount specified in the bill, or (b) if the person objects ... within the period of 7 business days
-- ... but has not referred the matter to the designated local regulatory authority or for costs assessment, and the period of 30
-- days after the later of the following dates has expired -- (i) the date on which the person was given the bill, (ii) the date on
-- which the person received an itemised bill following a request made in accordance with section 187 ..., or (c) if the money
-- otherwise becomes legally payable." r 42(4): whether or not a bill was given, "(a) if the money is withdrawn in accordance with
-- instructions that have been received by the law practice and that authorise the withdrawal, and (b) if, before effecting the
-- withdrawal, the law practice gives or sends to the person -- (i) a request for payment, referring to the proposed withdrawal, or
-- (ii) a written notice of withdrawal." r 42(5): the same notice where "the money is owed to the law practice by way of
-- reimbursement of money already paid by the law practice on behalf of the person".
-- "Business day" (s 6) is not computed: the number of business days since the bill is asked. Where more than one route is open,
-- the answer names the first in the rule's order (an ordering choice of this encoding).
DECLARE `My withdrawal` HAS
    `I gave a bill referring to the proposed withdrawal`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(3)
    `the date the bill was given`                                    IS A DATE
    `business days since the bill was given`                         IS A NUMBER   -- r 42(3)(a)
    `the client objected within 7 business days`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(3)(b)
    `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(3)(b)
    `the client asked for and received an itemised bill`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(3)(b)(ii)
    `the date the itemised bill was received`                        IS A DATE
    `the money has otherwise become legally payable`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(3)(c)
    `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(4)(a)
    `it reimburses money my firm paid for the client`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(5)(a)
    `I first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 42(4)(b), (5)(b)

DECLARE `Withdrawal answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: 7 business days have passed since the bill without objection (General Rules r 42(3)(a))`
    `yes: the client objected but has not referred it on, and 30 days have passed (r 42(3)(b))`
    `yes: the money has otherwise become legally payable (r 42(3)(c))`
    `yes: the client's instructions authorise it and the client was told first (r 42(4))`
    `yes: it reimburses money my firm paid for the client, and the client was told first (r 42(5))`
    `not yet`

@export May my firm pay its legal costs out of the client's trust money now (Uniform Law s 144(2)(b), General Rules r 42)?
GIVEN `the withdrawal` IS A `My withdrawal` @desc The bill, the client's response and any authority
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The date of the proposed withdrawal
GIVETH A `Withdrawal answer`
DECIDE `May my firm take its costs from trust money` IS
    IF     `the withdrawal`'s `I gave a bill referring to the proposed withdrawal`
       AND (NOT `the withdrawal`'s `the client objected within 7 business days`)
       AND `the withdrawal`'s `business days since the bill was given` AT LEAST 7
    THEN `yes: 7 business days have passed since the bill without objection (General Rules r 42(3)(a))`
    ELSE IF     `the withdrawal`'s `I gave a bill referring to the proposed withdrawal`
                 AND `the withdrawal`'s `the client objected within 7 business days`
                 AND (NOT `the withdrawal`'s `the client referred it to the Board or for costs assessment`)
                 AND Day `today` GREATER THAN `the later date` PLUS 30
         THEN `yes: the client objected but has not referred it on, and 30 days have passed (r 42(3)(b))`
         ELSE IF     `the withdrawal`'s `I gave a bill referring to the proposed withdrawal`
                      AND `the withdrawal`'s `the money has otherwise become legally payable`
              THEN `yes: the money has otherwise become legally payable (r 42(3)(c))`
              ELSE IF     `the withdrawal`'s `the client's instructions authorise the withdrawal`
                           AND `the withdrawal`'s `I first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`
                   THEN `yes: the client's instructions authorise it and the client was told first (r 42(4))`
                   ELSE IF     `the withdrawal`'s `it reimburses money my firm paid for the client`
                                AND `the withdrawal`'s `I first sent a request for payment or notice of withdrawal`
                        THEN `yes: it reimburses money my firm paid for the client, and the client was told first (r 42(5))`
                        ELSE `not yet`
    WHERE
        `the later date` MEANS
            IF     `the withdrawal`'s `the client asked for and received an itemised bill`
               AND Day (`the withdrawal`'s `the date the itemised bill was received`) GREATER THAN Day (`the withdrawal`'s `the date the bill was given`)
            THEN Day (`the withdrawal`'s `the date the itemised bill was received`)
            ELSE Day (`the withdrawal`'s `the date the bill was given`)

§§ `General Rules r 52 -- the client's trust account statement`

-- [General Rules] r 52(1): a statement must be given "to each person for whom or on whose behalf trust money (other than transit
-- money and written direction money) is held or controlled". r 52(4): it "is to be given -- (a) as soon as practicable after
-- completion of the matter ..., and (b) as soon as practicable after the person ... makes a reasonable request for the statement
-- during the course of the matter, and (c) except as provided by subrule (5) or (6), as soon as practicable after 30 June in each
-- year." r 52(5): no 30 June statement is needed "if at 30 June the balance of the ledger account or record is zero and -- (a) no
-- transaction affecting the ledger account or record has taken place within the previous 12 months, or (b) a trust account
-- statement has been furnished within the previous 12 months and no transaction ... has taken place since the last statement".
DECLARE `Statement occasion` IS ONE OF
    `the matter is complete`
    `the client reasonably asked during the matter`
    `30 June has passed`

DECLARE `My client's trust ledger` HAS
    `only transit money or written direction money`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 52(1)
    `the balance at 30 June was zero`                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 52(5)
    `no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 52(5)(a)
    `a statement was given in those 12 months and no transaction since` IS A BOOLEAN -- r 52(5)(b)

@export Must my firm give the client a trust account statement now (General Rules r 52)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `Statement occasion` @desc What has happened
      `the ledger` IS A `My client's trust ledger` @desc The client's trust ledger account
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my firm give the client a trust account statement` IF
        (NOT `the ledger`'s `only transit money or written direction money`)
    AND CONSIDER `the occasion`
        WHEN `30 June has passed` THEN
            NOT (    `the ledger`'s `the balance at 30 June was zero`
                 AND (   `the ledger`'s `no transaction in the 12 months before 30 June`
                      OR `the ledger`'s `a statement was given in those 12 months and no transaction since`))
        OTHERWISE TRUE
